  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:98102",
  "description": "Node.js is a software development platform for building fast and scalable network applications in the JavaScript programming language.   \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service via uncontrolled recursion in nested brace patterns (CVE-2026-102278)\n  * brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service via stack exhaustion from crafted brace patterns (CVE-2026-102276)\n  * undici: undici: Denial of Service via unhandled stream error on excessive content encodings (CVE-2026-109869)\n  * undici: undici: Denial of Service via TLS renegotiation with mismatched certificate (CVE-2026-87018)\n  * undici: undici: Certificate validation bypass via dropped TLS options in Agent (CVE-2026-109383)\n  * sqlite: sqlite: Denial of service via heap-based buffer overflow in FTS5 (CVE-2026-119373)\n  * sqlite: sqlite: Arbitrary code execution via crafted session changesets (CVE-2026-119379)\n  * sqlite: sqlite: Arbitrary code execution via corrupted FTS5 index (CVE-2026-119374)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
